798
00:29:35,310 --> 00:29:36,960
-My aunt will be so pleased.

799
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,050
I don't know how to thank you.

800
00:29:38,050 --> 00:29:40,640
-I should be delighted.

801
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:41,140
Oh.

802
00:29:41,140 --> 00:29:43,360
But you-- you haven't
 finished your drink.

803
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:44,700
-Drink the Blood of the Virgin!

804
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:46,120
Or am I coming on
 a little creepy?

805
00:29:46,120 --> 00:29:47,580
Sorry.

806
00:29:47,580 --> 00:29:49,040
-It's rather sweet.

807
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:50,050
-Oh, sorry.

808
00:29:50,050 --> 00:29:50,750
I gave you the Surge.

809
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:54,280
-Look into it.

810
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:56,450
-Virtually spotless.

811
00:29:56,450 --> 00:30:02,310
-So deep and rich
 and red and warm.

812
00:30:02,310 --> 00:30:03,280
-There's a bug in it.

813
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:07,670
-Deep, rich, red--

814
00:30:07,670 --> 00:30:09,130
-It's a blackberry.

815
00:30:09,130 --> 00:30:11,560
--warm.

816
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,590
-Uh, you know what?

817
00:30:12,590 --> 00:30:15,970
Uh, my aunt just called,
 and the ball's off.

818
00:30:15,970 --> 00:30:17,870
-Eh, you will come, then?

819
00:30:17,870 --> 00:30:19,530
-If you want me.

820
00:30:19,530 --> 00:30:20,740
-Saturday then.

821
00:30:20,740 --> 00:30:23,990
Um, after your performance
 here, we'll send a car.

822
00:30:23,990 --> 00:30:26,420
-Hey look, Rudy
 Vallee is the waiter.

823
00:30:26,420 --> 00:30:33,470
(SINGING) I'm just a vagabond,
 la-da, la-da-da-da-da--

824
00:30:33,470 --> 00:30:35,940
-Little bit of tap water from
 the basement sink, ma'am?

825
00:30:38,590 --> 00:30:39,810
-Come back in 15 seconds.

826
00:30:43,850 --> 00:30:44,490
-Hey, hey.

827
00:30:44,490 --> 00:30:45,190
It's Raoul.

828
00:30:45,190 --> 00:30:49,060
Me and Raoul, we're bodies.

829
00:30:49,060 --> 00:30:51,500
-Aunt Eva, this is
 your fourth drink.

830
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:52,230
-No, dear.

831
00:30:52,230 --> 00:30:52,970
It's my fifth.

832
00:30:52,970 --> 00:30:56,380
-Oh, you delightful,
 boozed-up old broad.

833
00:30:56,380 --> 00:30:59,070
The other day, I said the
 word "damn." [CHUCKLING].

834
00:31:01,650 --> 00:31:02,450
-Stay right there.

835
00:31:02,450 --> 00:31:03,320
Someone will scoop you up.

836
00:31:08,190 --> 00:31:10,280
-Enjoying yourself, darling?

837
00:31:10,280 --> 00:31:12,040
You're looking lovely.

838
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:12,540
-Thank you.

839
00:31:12,540 --> 00:31:14,520
-You're not, really.

840
00:31:14,520 --> 00:31:15,020
-Mark.

841
00:31:15,020 --> 00:31:15,500
-Hi.

842
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:16,000
-Hello.

843
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:19,360
-Mark, you're
 absolutely marvelous.

844
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:21,300
You're doing
 everything beautifully.

845
00:31:21,300 --> 00:31:25,160
You know, we've never
 had enough publicity.

846
00:31:25,160 --> 00:31:26,130
Now--

847
00:31:26,130 --> 00:31:28,410
VORELLI (OFFSCREEN): Marianne--

848
00:31:28,410 --> 00:31:29,440
-Oh, no.

849
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:32,290
I forgot the cheese tray.

850
00:31:32,290 --> 00:31:33,040
-She adores it.

851
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:33,700
-Don't worry.

852
00:31:33,700 --> 00:31:35,920
I will.

853
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,350
-Oh dear, I must go [INAUDIBLE].

854
00:31:38,350 --> 00:31:39,620
-You know, if not
 for alcohol, there'd

855
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:43,180
be no moisture in
 that woman at all.

856
00:31:43,180 --> 00:31:44,740
-Fever for the
 flavor of Pringles.

857
00:31:44,740 --> 00:31:45,530
Actual footage.

858
00:31:45,530 --> 00:31:46,030
-Hey.

859
00:31:46,030 --> 00:31:47,860
-Hm?

860
00:31:47,860 --> 00:31:50,150
Oh, nothing.

861
00:31:50,150 --> 00:31:51,780
Daydreaming, I suppose.

862
00:31:51,780 --> 00:31:54,520
-About this great "Are You
 Being Served" I saw last night.

863
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:55,740
-Mark, I don't like it.

864
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:56,240
-No?

865
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:57,830
Your aunt loves it.

866
00:31:57,830 --> 00:31:59,930
-She doesn't know what
 you're really here for.

867
00:31:59,930 --> 00:32:02,130
-Well, as long as I
 get the Vorelli story,

868
00:32:02,130 --> 00:32:02,870
what does it matter?

869
00:32:02,870 --> 00:32:05,320
-Oh, it's just-- I don't know.

870
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:08,260
I-- I wish I had never seen him.

871
00:32:08,260 --> 00:32:10,360
-Then I let the damn Tosca
 have it with my Weatherby.

872
00:32:13,290 --> 00:32:16,560
-Mark, when do I
 introduce Mr. Vorelli?

873
00:32:16,560 --> 00:32:18,340
-Right before he goes on.

874
00:32:18,340 --> 00:32:19,500
-It's about time now.

875
00:32:19,500 --> 00:32:22,190
-Oh, dear.

876
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:24,540
-Check it out, her hair acts
 like a smokeless ashtray.

877
00:32:24,540 --> 00:32:25,430
-Come on, don't worry.

878
00:32:25,430 --> 00:32:28,290
Everything will be all right.

879
00:32:28,290 --> 00:32:31,520
-Ladies and gentlemen, we have a
 great surprise for you tonight.

880
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:32,300
-My strip show.

881
00:32:32,300 --> 00:32:35,270
-Now, will everybody at the
 back please come forward.

882
00:32:35,270 --> 00:32:36,670
-Into the hot tub.

883
00:32:36,670 --> 00:32:38,110
-Thank you.

884
00:32:38,110 --> 00:32:41,440
And then I'd like you
 to form a semicircle.

885
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:42,470
-Five hours later.

886
00:32:42,470 --> 00:32:45,490
-I have much pleasure
 in presenting

887
00:32:45,490 --> 00:32:48,220
the great Vorelli and Hugo.

888
00:32:48,220 --> 00:32:51,720
-It's a dowager convention.

889
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:55,020
-Well, Hugo, I think you should
 sing a song for the audience.

890
00:32:55,020 --> 00:32:56,070
-No.

891
00:32:56,070 --> 00:32:57,430
I'm tired.

892
00:32:57,430 --> 00:33:00,080
-Well, you're in a surly mood.

893
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,460
I'm going to leave you alone.

894
00:33:01,460 --> 00:33:03,690
And when you're ready
 to perform, fine.

895
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:04,190
You've

896
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:05,980
-Hugo's got a John Agar smile.

897
00:33:05,980 --> 00:33:08,380
-Yes.

898
00:33:08,380 --> 00:33:11,280
-Duh--

899
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:14,390
-Pasty, pasty, beefy, pasty--

900
00:33:14,390 --> 00:33:16,050
-In the meantime,
 if you'll excuse me,

901
00:33:16,050 --> 00:33:17,130
I would like something to eat.

902
00:33:17,130 --> 00:33:20,140
I've just come from the
 theater, and I haven't had time.

903
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:23,210
-I think I'll have
 a vodka sandwich.

904
00:33:23,210 --> 00:33:25,570
-Oh, ham.

905
00:33:25,570 --> 00:33:27,170
I love it.

906
00:33:27,170 --> 00:33:29,840
-You cannibal.

907
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:31,290
-Well, what would you
 have to eat, Hugo,

908
00:33:31,290 --> 00:33:32,600
to make you a cannibal?

909
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:34,100
Sawdust?

910
00:33:34,100 --> 00:33:36,230
-Don't I get anything to eat?

911
00:33:36,230 --> 00:33:37,700
I'm hungry.

912
00:33:37,700 --> 00:33:40,060
-Whoever heard of a
 ventriloquist dummy eating?

913
00:33:40,060 --> 00:33:41,720
-My cousin knew a guy.

914
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:43,110
-I can eat.

915
00:33:43,110 --> 00:33:46,300
I can eat like you can.

916
00:33:46,300 --> 00:33:49,160
You are not the only
 one who likes to eat.

917
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:51,190
-Don't be ridiculous.

918
00:33:51,190 --> 00:33:52,310
-I'm hungry.

919
00:33:52,310 --> 00:33:54,490
I want something to eat.

920
00:33:54,490 --> 00:33:55,780
Now.

921
00:33:55,780 --> 00:33:59,410
-You surely don't expect
 me to wait on you.

922
00:33:59,410 --> 00:34:02,630
-Hugo's doing a Jack Benny take.

923
00:34:02,630 --> 00:34:03,660
-No.

924
00:34:03,660 --> 00:34:07,430
But I do want to eat.

925
00:34:07,430 --> 00:34:08,060
-Very well, then.

926
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:09,510
-Eat my shorts.

927
00:34:09,510 --> 00:34:13,400
-Get up and get it yourself.

928
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:16,250
-Sorry, ham.

929
00:34:16,250 --> 00:34:17,120
-Help me out here.

930
00:34:17,120 --> 00:34:19,010
Is it me or--

931
00:34:19,010 --> 00:34:19,690
-I'm pregnant.

932
00:34:22,490 --> 00:34:24,600
-OK, everybody thrill as
 I get my onion dip, OK?

933
00:34:28,250 --> 00:34:29,570
-You think he likes ham.

934
00:34:29,570 --> 00:34:31,200
Wait till you see me like ham.

935
00:34:35,250 --> 00:34:39,000
-You loogied on the salad.

936
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:42,070
-Don't drink too much, Hugo.

937
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:45,050
It might make the sawdust
 in your stomach swell.

938
00:34:45,050 --> 00:34:46,570
-But I took a Zantac.

939
00:34:46,570 --> 00:34:48,840
-You're a dummy, Hugo.

940
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:50,350
A common puppet.

941
00:34:58,220 --> 00:35:02,620
-(SINGING) Smile, though
 your heart is breaking.

942
00:35:02,620 --> 00:35:05,460
[SCREAMING]

943
00:35:05,460 --> 00:35:09,170
-Hugo, put down the knife.

944
00:35:09,170 --> 00:35:10,830
-Yeah, I'll put it
 down in your thigh.

945
00:35:10,830 --> 00:35:11,500
How about that?

946
00:35:11,500 --> 00:35:14,860
-I said, put it down.

947
00:35:14,860 --> 00:35:15,870
-Look familiar, Mike?

948
00:35:15,870 --> 00:35:16,450
-It may.

949
00:35:16,450 --> 00:35:16,950
Soon.

950
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:25,820
-You know, you
 frightened the ladies.

951
00:35:25,820 --> 00:35:29,070
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

952
00:35:29,070 --> 00:35:30,110
-Tell them you're sorry.

953
00:35:33,710 --> 00:35:37,700
-Look, Vorelli, jump
 up my wooden butt.

954
00:35:37,700 --> 00:35:40,080
-I am sorry.

955
00:35:40,080 --> 00:35:40,900
-You're all so ugly.

956
00:35:40,900 --> 00:35:41,860
Ha, ha!

957
00:35:41,860 --> 00:35:44,850
-Ladies and gentlemen.

958
00:35:44,850 --> 00:35:45,640
-And me.

959
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:50,100
-Yeah, what's up, Ron?

960
00:35:50,100 --> 00:35:51,530
Oh, I mean the Great Vorelli.

961
00:35:51,530 --> 00:35:52,490
-I--

962
00:35:52,490 --> 00:35:54,280
-Need changing.

963
00:35:54,280 --> 00:35:55,200
-Yes?

964
00:35:55,200 --> 00:35:57,350
Say it.

965
00:35:57,350 --> 00:36:02,240
-I am sorry.

966
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:03,940
-Master.

967
00:36:03,940 --> 00:36:06,140
-Look, I don't even want
 the damn sandwich anymore,

968
00:36:06,140 --> 00:36:07,280
all right?

969
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:08,940
-Master.

970
00:36:08,940 --> 00:36:11,710
-So his act is to get up
 and bicker with his doll.

971
00:36:11,710 --> 00:36:12,600
-Yeah.

972
00:36:12,600 --> 00:36:15,490
The Margaret Dumont Society
 expresses its appreciation.

973
00:36:15,490 --> 00:36:18,160
-And another $6 is
 raised for charity.

974
00:36:21,020 --> 00:36:22,470
-He went upstairs
 10 minutes ago.

975
00:36:22,470 --> 00:36:24,310
He should be back by now.

976
00:36:24,310 --> 00:36:26,880
If he does come
 down, I'm going up.

977
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:28,240
I've got to have a
 look at that dummy.

978
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:29,520
-Fred Sanford's son?

979
00:36:29,520 --> 00:36:30,020
-Dummy.

980
00:36:30,020 --> 00:36:32,460
-It just isn't possible.

981
00:36:32,460 --> 00:36:37,200
He must have someone inside
 it, like a small man or a boy.

982
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:39,160
That's the only explanation.

983
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:40,630
Either that, or it's mechanical.

984
00:36:40,630 --> 00:36:43,580
-Darling, it's absolutely
 thrilling, perfectly marvelous.

985
00:36:43,580 --> 00:36:45,790
-Oh, the mirabilia--
 have you ever

986
00:36:45,790 --> 00:36:48,000
seen anything so
 marvelous, Mark?

987
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:48,980
-No, never.

988
00:36:51,930 --> 00:36:53,880
Excuse me.

989
00:36:53,880 --> 00:36:54,410
Congratulations.

990
00:36:54,410 --> 00:36:57,630
-It would appear I'm
 at a major booty call.

991
00:36:57,630 --> 00:37:00,040
-Mr. Vorelli, you
 were magnificent.

992
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:01,490
-Thank you.

993
00:37:01,490 --> 00:37:02,450
-Come on, [ITALIAN].

994
00:37:06,790 --> 00:37:07,680
-[SPEAKING_ITALIAN]

995
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:09,860
-It's miked like an Altman film.

996
00:37:09,860 --> 00:37:11,250
-I think I should like a drink.

997
00:37:11,250 --> 00:37:12,640
Would you care to join me?

998
00:37:12,640 --> 00:37:14,040
This way.

999
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:14,590
-Thank you.

1000
00:37:14,590 --> 00:37:17,230
-Come on, it's much more
 depressing over here.

1001
00:37:17,230 --> 00:37:18,830
-What a wonderful performance.

1002
00:37:18,830 --> 00:37:20,210
-Yes, I've had him too.

1003
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:26,470
-I tell you, you only rent ham.

1004
00:37:31,060 --> 00:37:33,160
-That's the lowest door
 knob I've ever seen.

1005
00:37:36,630 --> 00:37:40,400
-So she won't let me play
 with your new Hot Wheels, huh?

1006
00:37:40,400 --> 00:37:41,610
-You know, this guy's lucky.

1007
00:37:41,610 --> 00:37:42,950
Hugo rarely gives interviews.

1008
00:37:46,640 --> 00:37:50,660
-That's not my call
 girl already, is it?

1009
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:52,130
-Bless me, puppet,
 for I have sinned.

1010
00:37:56,510 --> 00:37:59,880
-Oh, what are you-- what-- oh--
 fine, but I have a bad cold.

1011
00:38:04,430 --> 00:38:05,320
-What a complexion.

1012
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:06,890
Let me guess, you use
 Murphy's Oil Soap, right?

1013
00:38:10,190 --> 00:38:10,690
-Hey--

1014
00:38:14,380 --> 00:38:15,290
-Wow, wow.

1015
00:38:15,290 --> 00:38:15,790
Hey.

1016
00:38:15,790 --> 00:38:16,530
Wow.

1017
00:38:16,530 --> 00:38:17,180
Vorelli?

1018
00:38:17,180 --> 00:38:18,480
Vorelli?

1019
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:19,460
Ow!

1020
00:38:19,460 --> 00:38:21,430
[GARGLING]

1021
00:38:21,430 --> 00:38:23,510
-Weird, he's got
 marshmallow filling.

1022
00:38:26,240 --> 00:38:28,780
-When I call, he will come.

1023
00:38:28,780 --> 00:38:30,150
-He's talking to his poodle.

1024
00:38:30,150 --> 00:38:33,230
-Wherever you are,
 you will come.

1025
00:38:33,230 --> 00:38:34,150
[BARKING]

1026
00:38:34,150 --> 00:38:37,620
-But until I call,
 you will be yourself.

1027
00:38:37,620 --> 00:38:40,050
-An ugly pup-- oh,
 there I go again.

1028
00:38:40,050 --> 00:38:41,780
-Your usual, charming self.

1029
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:46,400
I must leave you now, my dear.

1030
00:38:46,400 --> 00:38:49,130
-I'm playing some
 kid's birthday party.

1031
00:38:49,130 --> 00:38:51,020
-Guten nacht.

1032
00:38:51,020 --> 00:38:51,520
[GERMAN]

1033
00:38:54,870 --> 00:38:55,610
-Ah, German.

1034
00:38:55,610 --> 00:38:58,320
The language of love.

1035
00:38:58,320 --> 00:38:59,290
-Your holiness.

1036
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:06,140
-I'm going to stop at the
 store on the way home tonight.

1037
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:08,360
Do we need milk?

1038
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:09,950
-I just have so
 much fun with him.

1039
00:39:09,950 --> 00:39:12,360
He knows how to make me laugh.

1040
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:14,450
-Take the ribbon from my hair.

1041
00:39:17,700 --> 00:39:19,890
-Even if a client brings
 in his vent figure,

1042
00:39:19,890 --> 00:39:21,590
we'll have a suit to fit him.

1043
00:39:21,590 --> 00:39:22,940
I guarantee it.

1044
00:39:25,860 --> 00:39:28,070
-You could park a Humvee
 in his chin dimple.

1045
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:32,600
-Don't even tell me you'll call.

1046
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:33,280
I know you won't.

1047
00:39:39,040 --> 00:39:41,040
[SIGHING]

1048
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:56,040
-Huh?

1049
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:59,040
Ah-- ah--

1050
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:07,580
-Did I just see someone
 walk in and paw my puppet?

1051
00:40:07,580 --> 00:40:10,180
-Maybe it should be chicken
 drummies instead of ham.

1052
00:40:10,180 --> 00:40:12,360
Maybe that would
 sell the bit better.

1053
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:15,250
Show that it's funny.

1054
00:40:15,250 --> 00:40:16,640
VORELLI (OFFSCREEN): Oh, baby.

1055
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:20,770
-Look, she has
 Hasidic wallpaper.

1056
00:40:20,770 --> 00:40:21,690
-Oh, look.

1057
00:40:21,690 --> 00:40:23,460
She has her bedtime
 false eyelashes on.

1058
00:40:28,790 --> 00:40:32,940
-(GASPING) I paid too
 much for my muffler.

1059
00:40:32,940 --> 00:40:34,800
-Oh, I hit the
 snooze button again.

1060
00:40:34,800 --> 00:40:35,570
I'll be late.

1061
00:40:35,570 --> 00:40:36,560
Better get up.

1062
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:39,510
-Marianne.

