2105
01:19:09,150 --> 01:19:10,260
-You're looking much better.

2106
01:19:10,260 --> 01:19:11,110
-Thank you.

2107
01:19:11,110 --> 01:19:14,090
The doctor took
 me off the drugs.

2108
01:19:14,090 --> 01:19:17,040
Mark, I-- I've got
 to talk to you.

2109
01:19:17,040 --> 01:19:17,940
-Hm?

2110
01:19:17,940 --> 01:19:20,400
-Hugo and I are engaged.

2111
01:19:20,400 --> 01:19:23,030
-I'm going away with Vorelli.

2112
01:19:23,030 --> 01:19:24,860
I'm in love with him.

2113
01:19:24,860 --> 01:19:26,240
-You're what?

2114
01:19:26,240 --> 01:19:27,670
-I'm in love with him.

2115
01:19:27,670 --> 01:19:28,790
-Look familiar, Mike?

2116
01:19:28,790 --> 01:19:31,080
Girls leaving you
 for ventriloquists?

2117
01:19:31,080 --> 01:19:32,940
-I'm sorry, Mark.

2118
01:19:32,940 --> 01:19:34,940
How can I explain?

2119
01:19:34,940 --> 01:19:37,870
It happened the
 night he stayed here.

2120
01:19:37,870 --> 01:19:41,590
I-- I just don't
 know what to say.

2121
01:19:44,510 --> 01:19:46,380
-First Robert
 Denby, and now you.

2122
01:19:49,550 --> 01:19:51,140
-Well, I have some
 muffins in the oven.

2123
01:19:54,280 --> 01:19:56,430
-Well, I'm going to
 go get a cheesy accent

2124
01:19:56,430 --> 01:20:00,470
and crepe beard and make
 her fall in love with me.

2125
01:20:00,470 --> 01:20:01,830
-Well, that was easy.

2126
01:20:01,830 --> 01:20:02,750
It was fun, in fact.

2127
01:20:09,780 --> 01:20:11,100
-Hey, look up there.

2128
01:20:11,100 --> 01:20:13,600
He flies Aunt Bea airlines.

2129
01:20:13,600 --> 01:20:16,490
-(FALSETTO) We'll be flying at
 a cruising altitude of 30,000

2130
01:20:16,490 --> 01:20:16,990
feet.

2131
01:20:16,990 --> 01:20:19,040
We may experience
 some turbulence.

2132
01:20:19,040 --> 01:20:21,630
Oh, Andy.

2133
01:20:21,630 --> 01:20:25,500
-Hey Vorelli, I had this
 corner all feng shuied.

2134
01:20:25,500 --> 01:20:25,990
-Uh, Vorelli?

2135
01:20:25,990 --> 01:20:27,200
Did you wear my yellow sweater?

2136
01:20:27,200 --> 01:20:28,910
Because I found
 it all pitted out.

2137
01:20:28,910 --> 01:20:30,590
Just-- just don't
 wear my stuff, OK?

2138
01:20:34,750 --> 01:20:36,200
-Maybe it's my new
 girlfriend or something,

2139
01:20:36,200 --> 01:20:38,410
but I feel great these days.

2140
01:20:38,410 --> 01:20:39,510
I just want to sing.

2141
01:20:43,210 --> 01:20:44,650
-Those pictures,
 where'd they come from?

2142
01:20:44,650 --> 01:20:48,310
Has be been in show
 business since 1830?

2143
01:20:48,310 --> 01:20:53,370
-Well, Hugo, tonight
 we fly to Spain.

2144
01:20:53,370 --> 01:20:57,170
And there, the very wealthy and
 beautiful Miss Marianne Horn

2145
01:20:57,170 --> 01:20:58,450
will become my bride.

2146
01:20:58,450 --> 01:21:00,730
-I want you to be my best man.

2147
01:21:00,730 --> 01:21:02,520
-Delicious thought.

2148
01:21:02,520 --> 01:21:06,960
-We'll give our last performance
 tonight and be on our way.

2149
01:21:06,960 --> 01:21:12,420
All four of us-- you,
 Hugo, my bride to be,

2150
01:21:12,420 --> 01:21:15,020
and my ugly little wooden lady.

2151
01:21:15,020 --> 01:21:16,780
-Hey, I like your mom.

2152
01:21:16,780 --> 01:21:22,460
-And then, after a few months,
 when my transfer is complete,

2153
01:21:22,460 --> 01:21:28,060
my beautiful young wife will
 die, leaving me all her money

2154
01:21:28,060 --> 01:21:31,980
and you an ugly little
 wooden companion.

2155
01:21:31,980 --> 01:21:33,740
[CHUCKLING]

2156
01:21:33,740 --> 01:21:38,310
-But then, you're
 ugly too, aren't you?

2157
01:21:38,310 --> 01:21:41,890
-Well, I think I do all
 right with what I have.

2158
01:21:41,890 --> 01:21:46,200
-(SINGING) It's quarter to 3:00,
 no one in the place but you

2159
01:21:46,200 --> 01:21:48,680
and rummy me.

2160
01:21:48,680 --> 01:21:49,750
-Could I have the same again?

2161
01:21:49,750 --> 01:21:53,190
-Make it a Samuel Stockbottom,
 double wheat cranberry lambic?

2162
01:21:53,190 --> 01:21:55,180
Thanks.

2163
01:21:55,180 --> 01:21:56,520
-Hey, look on the
 window back there.

2164
01:21:56,520 --> 01:21:57,470
It says midgets.

2165
01:21:57,470 --> 01:21:59,270
What is that a menu item?

2166
01:21:59,270 --> 01:22:01,910
-As long as they're boiled
 and come with chips, sure.

2167
01:22:05,150 --> 01:22:09,970
-Hey, could you flip on
 Monday Night Cricket, please?

2168
01:22:09,970 --> 01:22:13,000
-I lost my girlfriend, got
 in a fight with cigarettes.

2169
01:22:13,000 --> 01:22:17,060
Man, I miss those cigarettes.

2170
01:22:17,060 --> 01:22:19,510
-Ah, the bloody fool.

2171
01:22:19,510 --> 01:22:22,440
[INAUDIBLE] to do a lot
 of unnecessary expense

2172
01:22:22,440 --> 01:22:26,460
for an article about a
 charlatan-- a third-rate phony.

2173
01:22:26,460 --> 01:22:28,290
-Uh, sir, we were in this booth.

2174
01:22:28,290 --> 01:22:32,590
-The only woman I ever cared
 about falls in love with him.

2175
01:22:32,590 --> 01:22:34,270
If they don't fire
 me after this fiasco,

2176
01:22:34,270 --> 01:22:37,000
they're as crazy as I am.

2177
01:22:37,000 --> 01:22:38,180
-In fact, I'll
 just do it myself.

2178
01:22:38,180 --> 01:22:38,750
Me, you're fired.

2179
01:22:44,030 --> 01:22:46,690
-Sleep, my Marianne.

2180
01:22:46,690 --> 01:22:47,660
Deep--

2181
01:22:47,660 --> 01:22:48,300
-Purple.

2182
01:22:48,300 --> 01:22:48,890
-Deep--

2183
01:22:48,890 --> 01:22:49,430
-Cleaning.

2184
01:22:49,430 --> 01:22:50,640
-Sleep.

2185
01:22:50,640 --> 01:22:51,310
-It was.

2186
01:22:51,310 --> 01:22:53,650
Sheesh.

2187
01:22:53,650 --> 01:22:58,140
-(SNIFFING) It--
 it is me, isn't it?

2188
01:22:58,140 --> 01:22:59,120
Oh, yuck.

2189
01:23:03,050 --> 01:23:05,380
-Do you, Cathy Cathy,
 take Hugo to be

2190
01:23:05,380 --> 01:23:08,270
your lawfully wedded doll,
 to Pledge and behold,

2191
01:23:08,270 --> 01:23:09,580
to Finish and to Endust?

2192
01:23:09,580 --> 01:23:11,920
-Oh, Mike.

2193
01:23:11,920 --> 01:23:14,000
-Boss, can you at
 least change the paper

2194
01:23:14,000 --> 01:23:17,100
before you put her in here?

2195
01:23:17,100 --> 01:23:18,410
-You'll wake, my
 lovely Marianne,

2196
01:23:18,410 --> 01:23:22,040
after the performance tonight.

2197
01:23:22,040 --> 01:23:22,680
Hugo--

2198
01:23:22,680 --> 01:23:23,730
-Yo?

2199
01:23:23,730 --> 01:23:27,120
-You must behave when we
 give out last performance.

2200
01:23:27,120 --> 01:23:29,930
You've been getting out
 of control much too often.

2201
01:23:29,930 --> 01:23:31,820
-You've been eating way
 too much ham lately.

2202
01:23:34,410 --> 01:23:36,980
-You've been in your
 little wooden body so long,

2203
01:23:36,980 --> 01:23:38,740
you've become an
 individual again.

2204
01:23:38,740 --> 01:23:39,340
-Yeah, look at me.

2205
01:23:39,340 --> 01:23:42,350
I'm a real threat to you.

2206
01:23:42,350 --> 01:23:45,320
-No, it's much better over here.

2207
01:23:45,320 --> 01:23:46,930
-I think I must teach
 you a little lesson.

2208
01:23:46,930 --> 01:23:48,900
-I'm going to
 teach you to fetch.

2209
01:23:56,800 --> 01:23:57,430
-You're free to go.

2210
01:23:57,430 --> 01:23:58,900
Here's a little suit
 and a little $100 bill.

2211
01:23:58,900 --> 01:24:00,790
[KNOCKING]

2212
01:24:00,790 --> 01:24:02,720
-People for the Ethical
 Treatment of Puppets?

2213
01:24:02,720 --> 01:24:03,220
Hello?

2214
01:24:06,600 --> 01:24:09,320
-I am disciplining my puppet.

2215
01:24:09,320 --> 01:24:11,230
-Ah, dear Grace.

2216
01:24:11,230 --> 01:24:12,180
-Attica!

2217
01:24:12,180 --> 01:24:13,590
Attica!

2218
01:24:13,590 --> 01:24:15,550
-I thought you wanted me now.

2219
01:24:15,550 --> 01:24:18,000
-Not now, dear.

2220
01:24:18,000 --> 01:24:20,330
I have a few things to
 clear up with the manager

2221
01:24:20,330 --> 01:24:22,280
before I leave.

2222
01:24:22,280 --> 01:24:23,560
I shall come to your room.

2223
01:24:23,560 --> 01:24:24,290
-Don't be long.

2224
01:24:24,290 --> 01:24:27,350
-As soon as I'm
 through with him.

2225
01:24:27,350 --> 01:24:29,550
-I've just got to get something
 out of the hamper here,

2226
01:24:29,550 --> 01:24:30,870
if you don't mind.

2227
01:24:30,870 --> 01:24:31,440
Ah, there you go.

2228
01:24:31,440 --> 01:24:31,940
Thanks.

2229
01:24:34,440 --> 01:24:36,230
-Hugo.

2230
01:24:36,230 --> 01:24:38,610
I'm your master.

2231
01:24:38,610 --> 01:24:44,260
Get back in your cage,
 or I will destroy you.

2232
01:24:44,260 --> 01:24:45,610
[SCREAMING]

2233
01:24:45,610 --> 01:24:47,870
-Oh, for the love of--

2234
01:24:47,870 --> 01:24:50,210
-This has to be stressful, but
 Hugo's more chipper than ever.

2235
01:24:52,980 --> 01:24:55,010
-He looks like Burgess
 Meredith all of a sudden.

2236
01:25:00,040 --> 01:25:00,540
-Aha!

2237
01:25:00,540 --> 01:25:02,400
It's a wooden chair,
 and all finished

2238
01:25:02,400 --> 01:25:06,860
wooden products are my brother,
 and they will protect me.

2239
01:25:06,860 --> 01:25:09,990
-Thomas Peter Vorelli,
 you be nice to your toys.

2240
01:25:13,230 --> 01:25:14,270
-OK, OK.

2241
01:25:14,270 --> 01:25:16,910
You are going to get it so--
 oh, you son of a-- come here.

2242
01:25:16,910 --> 01:25:17,890
Come here.

2243
01:25:17,890 --> 01:25:20,190
-You know, you guys,
 I just remembered,

2244
01:25:20,190 --> 01:25:22,010
I gave a devil doll
 to my niece once.

2245
01:25:22,010 --> 01:25:23,900
-Uh-oh.

2246
01:25:23,900 --> 01:25:26,130
-This is going to make
 tonight's show pretty tense.

2247
01:25:30,120 --> 01:25:32,880
-Don't ask me.

2248
01:25:32,880 --> 01:25:33,770
-You see, Vorelli?

2249
01:25:33,770 --> 01:25:34,720
I'm pretty strong.

2250
01:25:34,720 --> 01:25:37,340
I've been doing
 push-ups in my cage.

2251
01:25:37,340 --> 01:25:37,840
Ha, ha.

2252
01:25:37,840 --> 01:25:39,210
I don't even have a trachea.

2253
01:25:44,320 --> 01:25:49,300
-(SINGING) Memories light
 the corners of my mind.

2254
01:25:49,300 --> 01:25:51,790
Misty--

2255
01:25:51,790 --> 01:25:52,790
-Kennel, Hugo.

2256
01:25:52,790 --> 01:25:54,710
Kennel.

2257
01:25:54,710 --> 01:25:56,400
-I've got to get that
 training collar for him.

2258
01:26:00,220 --> 01:26:01,770
-And ladies and gentlemen,
 that is our story.

2259
01:26:01,770 --> 01:26:05,420
A cautionary tale
 to be sure, but--

2260
01:26:05,420 --> 01:26:05,920
-Hm.

2261
01:26:05,920 --> 01:26:07,090
So is he being Martinized?

2262
01:26:07,090 --> 01:26:08,490
-No, I think it's the
 shroud of Vorelli.

2263
01:26:12,410 --> 01:26:14,980
-What the-- you know,
 where did that come from?

2264
01:26:14,980 --> 01:26:16,640
I mean, what was that about?

2265
01:26:19,290 --> 01:26:21,130
-Next time I'm just
 gonna lease a dummy.

2266
01:26:21,130 --> 01:26:23,680
It's such a headache to own.

2267
01:26:23,680 --> 01:26:25,190
-Beanie babies don't
 get this kind of power.

2268
01:26:28,910 --> 01:26:30,560
-I'm sweaty because I
 was choking a puppet.

2269
01:26:30,560 --> 01:26:31,060
No.

2270
01:26:31,060 --> 01:26:32,040
No, wait--

2271
01:26:32,040 --> 01:26:34,410
-Don't be alarmed, Mr. English.

2272
01:26:34,410 --> 01:26:36,510
Vorelli is now a wooden doll.

2273
01:26:36,510 --> 01:26:38,760
-Actually, I just
 left my hat in here.

2274
01:26:38,760 --> 01:26:41,270
-I am his master.

2275
01:26:41,270 --> 01:26:44,910
The tables are turned.

2276
01:26:44,910 --> 01:26:47,580
You need have no
 fear for Marianne.

2277
01:26:47,580 --> 01:26:50,090
She is sleeping peacefully.

2278
01:26:50,090 --> 01:26:53,940
When I wake her, she
 will be her normal self.

2279
01:26:53,940 --> 01:26:55,260
-What?

2280
01:26:55,260 --> 01:26:58,600
-Mr. English, get
 me out of here.

2281
01:26:58,600 --> 01:27:00,610
I am the Great Vorelli.

2282
01:27:00,610 --> 01:27:02,570
He can't do this to me.

2283
01:27:02,570 --> 01:27:03,590
Please.

2284
01:27:03,590 --> 01:27:04,780
-Really ironic, huh?

2285
01:27:04,780 --> 01:27:06,570
-Mr. English, don't
 let him do it.

2286
01:27:06,570 --> 01:27:07,450
-Don't you think?

2287
01:27:07,450 --> 01:27:09,480
-I'll do anything you say.

2288
01:27:09,480 --> 01:27:11,440
Get me out of here.

2289
01:27:11,440 --> 01:27:13,580
I'll do anything you say.

2290
01:27:13,580 --> 01:27:14,330
Please.

2291
01:27:14,330 --> 01:27:15,800
I am the--

2292
01:27:15,800 --> 01:27:16,410
-Great Vorelli.

2293
01:27:16,410 --> 01:27:16,900
-Great Vorelli.

2294
01:27:16,900 --> 01:27:18,500
-Great Vorelli, right.

2295
01:27:18,500 --> 01:27:20,850
-On the other hand, it's
 kind of a cute, little body.

2296
01:27:20,850 --> 01:27:22,350
You know, just comb its hair.

2297
01:27:22,350 --> 01:27:24,590
-Hugo the dummy was
 arraigned in Superior Court,

2298
01:27:24,590 --> 01:27:25,680
county of Los Angeles.

2299
01:27:25,680 --> 01:27:27,990
In a moment, the
 results of that trial.

2300
01:27:27,990 --> 01:27:30,080
-You know, I gotta
 admit, this really

2301
01:27:30,080 --> 01:27:32,630
does cut into my deep
 love of ventriloquy.

2302
01:27:32,630 --> 01:27:34,480
-Why don't you give
 us "ham" moment?

2303
01:27:47,110 --> 01:27:51,040
-Oh, you're an ugly little
 dummy, aren't you, Mike-o?

2304
01:27:51,040 --> 01:27:56,630
An ugly, smelly, horrible little
 dummy, stuffed with sawdust.

2305
01:27:56,630 --> 01:27:59,190
A dummy who will never
 have ham-- certainly

2306
01:27:59,190 --> 01:28:01,590
not unless he gets it himself.

2307
01:28:01,590 --> 01:28:04,190
A dummy who will
 never drink wine.

2308
01:28:04,190 --> 01:28:05,680
Yes, a horrible, smelly, ugly--

2309
01:28:05,680 --> 01:28:06,330
-Crow?

2310
01:28:06,330 --> 01:28:06,930
--stupid--

2311
01:28:06,930 --> 01:28:08,440
-Crow, what's-- what's going on?

2312
01:28:08,440 --> 01:28:09,390
Why am I in a cage?

2313
01:28:09,390 --> 01:28:10,720
Why am I dressed like Hugo?

2314
01:28:10,720 --> 01:28:12,430
-Not only can't
 you have ham, you

2315
01:28:12,430 --> 01:28:14,340
can't have any luncheon meats.

2316
01:28:14,340 --> 01:28:16,370
Not bologna or Feringa.

2317
01:28:16,370 --> 01:28:18,170
Not even cotto salami.

2318
01:28:18,170 --> 01:28:19,150
Why?

2319
01:28:19,150 --> 01:28:22,000
Because luncheon meats make
 the sawdust in your stomach

2320
01:28:22,000 --> 01:28:22,710
explode.

2321
01:28:22,710 --> 01:28:23,990
-Crow.

2322
01:28:23,990 --> 01:28:24,510
-What?

2323
01:28:24,510 --> 01:28:25,010
What?

2324
01:28:25,010 --> 01:28:26,620
-Now, this is really too much.

2325
01:28:26,620 --> 01:28:29,680
I fall asleep so you
 build a cage around me,

2326
01:28:29,680 --> 01:28:31,790
and then you dress me up
 as Hugo the devil doll,

2327
01:28:31,790 --> 01:28:34,240
and you whisper odd,
 irrelevant taunts at me?

2328
01:28:34,240 --> 01:28:34,870
-What?

2329
01:28:34,870 --> 01:28:36,150
What is wrong with that?

2330
01:28:36,150 --> 01:28:38,060
Mike, I feel like I
 can't do anything today,

2331
01:28:38,060 --> 01:28:39,610
and you are all over me.

2332
01:28:39,610 --> 01:28:40,250
Boy.

2333
01:28:40,250 --> 01:28:41,950
-(HUMMING) Well, now that
 my soul's in this toaster

2334
01:28:41,950 --> 01:28:42,450
strudel--

2335
01:28:42,450 --> 01:28:43,020
-Say!

2336
01:28:43,020 --> 01:28:44,950
--and I've got
 these killer gams,

2337
01:28:44,950 --> 01:28:46,760
I'm ready to be your
 leggy assistant.

2338
01:28:46,760 --> 01:28:47,260
-Oh.

2339
01:28:47,260 --> 01:28:47,710
No.

2340
01:28:47,710 --> 01:28:48,280
No, look at this.

2341
01:28:48,280 --> 01:28:48,850
Look.

2342
01:28:48,850 --> 01:28:49,500
-What?

2343
01:28:49,500 --> 01:28:52,060
Boy Mike, you know,
 what is wrong with that?

2344
01:28:52,060 --> 01:28:53,170
You can't be serious.

2345
01:28:53,170 --> 01:28:54,840
-A-Pearl-o, take me away.

2346
01:28:54,840 --> 01:28:58,440
-You know, it is your problem
 at this point, Nelson, not mine.

2347
01:28:58,440 --> 01:28:59,020
Good luck.

2348
01:28:59,020 --> 01:29:00,920
-I'm gonna be physically ill.

2349
01:29:00,920 --> 01:29:04,600
-Oh, like you got any right
 to belly-ache, Smell-son.

2350
01:29:04,600 --> 01:29:08,140
I had to watch some idiot
 mad god get eaten by a lion

2351
01:29:08,140 --> 01:29:13,300
and put up with this
 Etruscan windbag here.

2352
01:29:13,300 --> 01:29:17,380
-Citizens, as you may
 notice, I'm wearing pants.

2353
01:29:17,380 --> 01:29:19,880
Thanks to the gods.

2354
01:29:19,880 --> 01:29:21,750
I'd like to thank you
 all for coming here

2355
01:29:21,750 --> 01:29:24,330
to Lesser God Day
 at the Colosseum.

2356
01:29:24,330 --> 01:29:27,500
Now, before our mad goth
 doth his enemies vanquish,

2357
01:29:27,500 --> 01:29:30,430
I think it both meet and
 right that we recognize

2358
